cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as described below."
type: software
title: "A Theory-Informed Agent-Based Model of Context-Dependent Physical Activity Decisions"
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: 2026-07-13

authors:
  - family-names: "Reinalter"
    given-names: "Raphael"
    affiliation: "Institute of Sport Science, University of Bern"

abstract: >
  This repository contains a theory-informed and modular agent-based
  simulation framework developed as part of a master's thesis at the
  University of Bern. The framework integrates heterogeneous synthetic
  agents, hourly activity schedules, environmental conditions, spatial
  accessibility, energy levels, psychological constructs, and a
  large-language-model-supported decision pipeline. It generates daily
  physical activity decisions, diary entries, and longitudinal updates
  of psychological states. The repository also contains the analysis
  scripts, prompts, and tests used in the thesis.

keywords:
  - agent-based modeling
  - physical activity
  - mobile health
  - large language models

repository-code: "https://github.com/Rapha1337/MScThesis"
